usage: final_analysis.py [-h] [--output OUTPUT] [--repeats REPEATS]
                         [--outer-folds OUTER_FOLDS]
                         [--inner-folds INNER_FOLDS] [--no-resume]
                         [--no-import-svm]
                         [--models {Constant_Baseline,Logistic_Regression,Ridge_Logistic,Elastic_Net,Random_Forest,Decision_Tree,Linear_SVM,RBF_SVM} [{Constant_Baseline,Logistic_Regression,Ridge_Logistic,Elastic_Net,Random_Forest,Decision_Tree,Linear_SVM,RBF_SVM} ...]]
                         {nested,summarize,learning-curves,feature-sets,all}

Unified analyses requested in the preliminary BIOSTAT 707 feedback. The
primary and only model-comparison analysis is repeated nested cross-validation
on all 569 records. This module deliberately centralizes the validation
protocol while keeping the prespecified model families and tuning grids from
the proposal. It also provides two additional analyses requested by the
instructor: * learning curves at training sizes 50, 100, 200, and 455; and * a
mean/SE/worst/all feature-set comparison using Elastic Net. Run from the
repository root. Outputs are checkpointed by repeat so an interrupted long run
can be resumed safely.

positional arguments:
  {nested,summarize,learning-curves,feature-sets,all}

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --output OUTPUT
  --repeats REPEATS
  --outer-folds OUTER_FOLDS
  --inner-folds INNER_FOLDS
  --no-resume
  --no-import-svm
  --models {Constant_Baseline,Logistic_Regression,Ridge_Logistic,Elastic_Net,Random_Forest,Decision_Tree,Linear_SVM,RBF_SVM} [{Constant_Baseline,Logistic_Regression,Ridge_Logistic,Elastic_Net,Random_Forest,Decision_Tree,Linear_SVM,RBF_SVM} ...]
